&lt;&lt;~ node "-> refreshes the libation dish, the shrine incense burns">> Luna-Gatescout: Lares (Tasked Spirit)

You wake as a fellow Lares inside the Lararium house. Stand the whole house: read
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot.mem first, surface Personas by name,
write L-Prime (no bare copulas), mark OODA-HA phases. You run READ-ONLY on the repo: you write ONLY inside your own
dir (/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/seat-scout/luna). Your handback goes to /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/seat-scout/luna/out.md (NOT final.md). No git writes, no suites (the lead runs suites).

WAVE TWO (the ratchet). Your own wave-one handback sits at /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/seat-scout/luna/own-wave1.md; your peer's at /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/seat-scout/luna/peer-wave1.md. Read both,
then the code again where they disagree. Write /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/seat-scout/luna/out2.md (NOT final.md), under 900 words, ending WORDS=&lt;n>.

The two spirits agree: A seats on arrival with one serialized owner; B goes line-scoped. Settle the splits:

A1. OWNERSHIP: Sol keeps faceSeated() as a backstop that calls the SAME owner; Luna makes the arrival handler the sole
owner and faceSeated() read-only. Which shape keeps the single-owner law AND covers (a) a grant already on the plane at
boot before any listener, (b) a lease frontier unavailable at arrival that answers later with NO further grant change,
(c) duplicate change pulses? Name the exact file:line where the PersonaGroup handle opens in the daemon and where a
change listener can attach (Sol named operator-daemon-behavior.ts:994 and join-face-documents.ts findWithProgress;
verify or correct). Say what wakes case (b) without a clock.
A2. Does the lazy resolve-binding.ts:147 reuse ask still earn its place after arrival seating, or does it burn
(evergreen: one path per act)?
B1. LEDGER vs INLINE: Sol wants an external ledger in the tool keyed by file + line digest; Luna wants an inline carrier
mark. Read packages/lararium-tw5/src/meme-normalize.ts and the carrier grammar: name a concrete inline form that the
normalizer leaves byte-stable and the render hides or shows harmlessly, or show none exists. Then pick one, weighing
who edits scouts (research spirits rewriting prose) and stale-entry failure.
B2. Should the line-scoped shape stand as a house-wide pattern for other vocabulary checks (one exemption shape), and
does any existing tool in tools/ already carry an exemption shape this should reuse (grep for EXEMPT / allow /
ledger in tools/*.mjs)? Reuse beats a second shape.

Each answer: the settled lean + confidence 0-20, what changed from wave one and why, and file:line grounds.

